Chapter 37: The Void-Mesh Harness
The air in the Void-Forge was stifling, radiating a dry, oppressive heat that shimmered against the lead-shielded walls. At the center of the subterranean workshop stood a massive plasma furnace fueled by dense liquid mana, glowing with an intense, violet luminescence. beside it lay a massive anvil forged from dark, light-absorbing meteor iron.
Kaelen removed his coat, revealing his lean, hyper-dense physique. Under the forge's harsh light, his sub-dermal [Obsidian Hard-Plating] gave his skin a faint, metallic sheen.
He spread the Scales of the Void-Dragon blueprint across a heat-resistant slate table, memorizing the intricate weaving pattern in seconds. The schematic required fusing the high-density Void-Scale Hydra Plates with melted Kinetic Steel and utilizing Hydra Fangs as an essence catalyst to bind the structure at a molecular level.
Kaelen didn't waste time with manual bellows or mechanical tongs.
He retrieved twelve pristine Void-Scale Plates and three Hydra Fangs from his spatial salvage inventory, placing them directly into the furnace's crucible alongside a block of high-grade Kinetic Steel.
WHIRRRR!
He engaged the plasma controls, ramping the temperature to over three thousand degrees. The furnace roared, its violet flames turning white-hot as the high-tier materials began to soften.
Standard smiths required heavy hydraulic hammers and hours of heating cycles to shape Tier-B materials. Kaelen had something far more precise: his bare hands, backed by 101 Strength and 89 Aetheric Resonance.
Using heavy tungsten tongs, Kaelen pulled the glowing, semi-molten mass of Void-Scale alloy from the furnace and slammed it onto the meteor-iron anvil.
CLANG!
The concussive impact vibrated through the lead-shielded chamber.
Kaelen didn't use a hammer. He channeled a micro-pulse of his [Abyssal Shell Resonance] directly into his right fist, striking the molten metal with surgical, rhythmic precision.
BOOM! CLANG! BOOM!
Each blow struck with the force of an industrial steam press. Under his continuous, high-density kinetic strikes, the thick obsidian plates flattened, thinning into ultra-dense, interlocking metallic scales no thicker than a coin.
He picked up the three glowing Hydra Fangs, crushing them in his left hand into a fine, sparkling essence powder. He sprinkled the catalyst over the red-hot scale weave, channeling his 89 Aetheric Resonance to bind the essence into the metal.
The molten scales hissed violently, absorbing the dark purple essence. The alloy transformed before his eyes, shifting from rigid iron into a liquid-smooth, dark obsidian mesh that rippled like silk.
Using the blueprint's precise weaving instructions, Kaelen shaped the metallic mesh into a full chest-and-back harness with flexible shoulder straps and rib guards.
After quenching the glowing harness in a bath of anti-mana cooling oil, Kaelen pulled the finished piece from the vat.
[Crafting Complete!]
 * Item Forged: [Hydra's Void-Scale Harness (Concealed)]
 * Quality: Tier-B Elite (Custom Masterwork)
 * Properties:
   * Sub-Dermal Flexibility: Weighs less than two pounds; conforms invisibly beneath ordinary clothing.
   * Kinetic & Elemental Absorption: Reduces incoming blunt, cutting, piercing, and elemental damage to the chest and vital organs by 40%.
   * Resonance Synergy: Amplifies passive trait [Hydra's Vital Regeneration] by an additional +25\%.
   * Concealment: Disguised with grey corrosion-paint; completely invisible to standard biometric scans.
Kaelen lifted the lightweight obsidian harness. The dark mesh felt cool and supple to the touch, resembling fine, dark chainmail coated in smooth dragon scales.
He slipped the harness over his bare shoulders, adjusting the side straps.
CLICK.
The harness tightened automatically, moulding itself seamlessly across his chest, back, and ribs like a second skin. When he pulled his standard Anvil Ridge uniform and utility vest back over his upper body, there was zero bulk—no outline, no stiffness, no indication that he was wearing high-grade Tier-B armor.
Kaelen raised his right fist, testing his range of motion. His movement was completely uninhibited. His 102 Agility felt as fluid and effortless as ever.
Combined with his passive [Obsidian Hard-Plating] (50% physical damage reduction) and his new [Hydra's Void-Scale Harness] (40% damage absorption), his chest was now virtually impenetrable to anything short of a direct Tier-A kinetic strike.
Kaelen picked up his coat, pulled his hood low over his eyes, and walked toward the steel elevator.
His gear was forged, his stats were past the hundred-point mark, and his pockets held over six hundred thousand credits.
It was time to step out of the dark and report back for Squad 4's first field deployment.
